---
title: Analytics
---

An analytics plugin computes custom metrics, charts and insights for a single
exercise over its whole history. The user picks one in **Settings → Analytics**;
it renders on the exercise detail page.

## The contract

```ts
export const pluginBundle = {
  formatVersion: 1,
  pluginId: "com.you.volume",
  family: "analytics",
  entryExport: "analytics",
} as const;

export const analytics = {
  id: "com.you.volume",
  name: "Weekly Volume",
  description: "Total tonnage per week.",
  metricDefinitions: [
    { id: "weeklyVolume", label: "Weekly volume", unit: "kg" },
  ],

  compute(input) {
    const byWeek = new Map();
    for (const entry of input.history) {
      const wk = Math.floor(entry.performedAtMs / (7 * 864e5));
      const vol = entry.sets.reduce((s, x) => s + x.weight * x.reps, 0);
      byWeek.set(wk, (byWeek.get(wk) ?? 0) + vol);
    }
    const points = [...byWeek.entries()]
      .sort((a, b) => a[0] - b[0])
      .map(([wk, v]) => ({ date: wk * 7 * 864e5, value: v }));

    return {
      metrics: [{ id: "weeklyVolume", value: points.at(-1)?.value ?? 0 }],
      series: [{ metricId: "weeklyVolume", label: "Weekly volume", points }],
      insights: points.length > 1 && points.at(-1).value > points.at(-2).value
        ? ["Volume up week over week"]
        : [],
    };
  },
};
```

## Input & output

`compute(input: AnalyticsInput)` — `@logit/core/domain/analytics`.

- **`input.history`** — `ExerciseHistoryEntry[]`, **oldest first**, all available.
- **`input.exercise`** — `{ name, id?, exerciseType? }`.

```ts
type AnalyticsOutput = {
  metrics: { id: string; value: number | string; formatted?: string }[];
  series: { metricId: string; label: string; points: { date: number; value: number }[] }[];
  insights?: string[];
  label?: string;
};
```

`metricDefinitions` (id + label + optional `unit` / `higherIsBetter`) is read
from a `meta` call at install and shown in the picker.

Nutrition analytics ([`nutrition-analytics`](/docs/plugins/nutrition)) has the
same shape over diary + weight data.
